  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In the 1950s, the story goes, a man named Townsend found a kind of bismuth, a heavy metal, that was pushed away instead of pulled in. If true, that would hint that someone was chasing a way to cancel gravity. Michels tells it himself in three episodes, quoting Louis Witten, a physicist then at the Martin Company, from an interview Witten gave the American Institute of Physics (in one telling Michels calls the source \"American theoretical physics\"). In one episode he ties the name to Thomas Townsend Brown, a researcher who is the subject of one of his documentaries."
}
